      "category": "characterization",
      "trigger": "When identifying the nature of a large unilateral thoracic opacity on a chest X-ray.",
      "steps": [
        "Assess the opacity for features distinguishing a mediastinal mass with secondary lung collapse from primary parenchymal disease (e.g., look for loss of normal mediastinal contours, displacement of structures, or a 'D-shaped' density merging with the hilum).",
        "Differentiate from other causes of whiteout such as massive pleural effusion (which typically shows a meniscus and contralateral shift) or simple pneumonia (which usually preserves mediastinal borders and lacks a discrete mass effect)."
      ]
    }
